{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1095458-why-m-taw-resonates-with-me-and-probably-several-others","id":1095458,"title":"Why M:tAw Resonates with Me (And Probably Several Others)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-22T06:13:42-07:00","id":1095458,"title":"Why M:tAw Resonates with Me (And Probably Several Others)","content":"Ever since I began reading the 1st edition corebook of Mage: the Awakening back in mid-2014, I was instantly hooked. Since then, I've bought several supplements of it, still looking at getting more, played in several chronicles, and setting a chronicle myself. One thing is certainly clear: I. Love. Mage. When I first read the corebook, I couldn\u2019t put my finger on it, but the game spoke to me on a deep level. Now that I am more learned, I\u2019ve begun to point my finger on all the different aspects that relate to me, as well as quite a few others.<br /> <br /> Alright, I\u2019m just gonna say it and it doesn\u2019t matter to me how you react: I am a sorcerer. Yes, I mean someone who practices actual magic, casts spells, enchants items, etc. No, I am not someone who dabbles in New Age mumbo-jumbo mistaken as occult practices, I use real magic.<br /> <br /> <b>What is \u201cReal Magic\u201d?</b><br /> Now, it\u2019s important to note what I actually mean by \u201creal magic\u201d, since there are so many conceptions of it. Thankfully, real magic isn\u2019t like Supernal magic (though there are some commonalities, which I\u2019ll get to later). It\u2019s not flashes, bangs, and rapid physical transformations, it\u2019s much more subtle than that. Conceptually speaking, The Force from Star Wars is pretty accurate. While it\u2019s certainly not gonna let you make force grips or sprout lightning from your fingers, it is certainly about manipulating the natural energy that permeates throughout all life and the world, and can guide you in ways that pure logic and reason simply can\u2019t. Another accurate depiction can be seen in the film Spirited Away, which comes as no surprise since it was literally made as an instruction manual for magic (but that\u2019s for another thread).<br /> <br /> Real magic is not supernatural in nature (I suppose you could argue that it\u2019s paranormal, but I wouldn\u2019t say that\u2019s completely accurate), nor is it loud, glittery, or rare. It\u2019s as common as birches, and just as natural and showy. It does involve spirits, and you might argue that would make it supernatural, but I would argue that spirits are also perfectly natural as well, they just happen to be incorporeal is all.<br /> <br /> <b>Who Are Sorcerers?</b><br /> Now that real magic has been defined, what exactly is a sorcerer? Sorcerers are simply people who have magical talents and are more sensitive to spiritual activity. That\u2019s really all there is to it, no deals with the devil, no superpowers, just people who happen to have talents and senses most do not, just as they lack talents many others have.<br /> <br /> Being a sorcerer myself, I can sense things like spirits and I have some magical talents (I\u2019m particularly good with divination, which is a generic term for gathering information in general, not just telling the future), but I\u2019m no good at sports and I\u2019m anosmic (I have no sense of smell).<br /> <br /> In other words, sorcerers aren\u2019t special; we\u2019re just like you. You may not be able to speak with spirits.... but there\u2019s probably something you can do that I can\u2019t.<br /> <br /> <b>I Don\u2019t Believe You</b><br /> That\u2019s fine, and to be fair, your disbelief is probably a rational reaction. That doesn\u2019t mean you\u2019re right, but you\u2019re not being irrational, either. How does that make sense? Lemme explain:<br /> <br /> What is the world to a mole? Dark, cramped, a series of chambers and burrows, and colored with scents. Where then, do stars fit in the picture? They don\u2019t. You can try to explain what they are, how they form, what they do, etc. but at the end of the day, all you\u2019ll wind up doing is wasting your time and frustrating the mole. It can\u2019t sense them in any way and they don\u2019t impact its life in any significant way.<br /> <br /> Does that mean stars don\u2019t exist? Of course not, but damned if you\u2019re gonna convince the mole they do, let alone teach it astronomy. Same deal with magic. Most people can\u2019t sense the phenomena that sorcerers do in any real, significant way. The best they can get is a few hints here and there; and usually only in places where such things concentrate, much in the same manner as the mole feeling the sun\u2019s heat through the earth when it\u2019s close to the surface.<br /> <br /> So, much like the mole, disbelief of magic is a rational reaction for those who are not sensitive to it. But just because you can't sense it, doesn\u2019t mean it isn\u2019t there.<br /> <br /> <b>Awakened &amp; Sleepers</b><br /> Now that we\u2019ve got all that outta the way, it\u2019s time to get into the meat of this thread: how Mage: the Awakening relates to real-life magic and sorcerers.<br /> <br /> We\u2019ll start with the difference between the Awakened and Sleepers. While you\u2019ve probably already noted that the Awakened have many differences to what I described with real-life sorcerers, there are some correlations. For starters, the Awakened have senses that Sleepers simply do not: they see the invisible and hear the inaudible, much in the same way that sorcerers are more sensitive to things outside of purely material existence.<br /> <br /> Sleepers are like the mole in the above analog;, they simply can\u2019t sense the supernatural like the Awakened can. Sure, there\u2019s no Sleeping Curse that harms non-sorcerers when they\u2019re faced with magic or anything, but the alienation that the Awakened suffer is a common experience for sorcerers, especially in this day and age.<br /> <br /> <b>The Lie</b><br /> While the real world is no illusion, there\u2019s certainly more to it than most people acknowledge, especially in the western world. Much of modern society says that magic isn\u2019t real, that science is the be-all and end-all of truth. If you think magic is real, then you clearly need to be reeducated.... in the psych ward. Okay, that\u2019s a bit of an exaggeration, but not by much.<br /> <br /> There\u2019s a very real denial of magic in today\u2019s world; those who practice it are often ridiculed and sometimes even ostracized. Most sorcerers don\u2019t even realize their magical potential, simply because they\u2019ve been told all their life that magic isn\u2019t real, so they disbelieve it themselves, even if their senses are literally telling them otherwise.<br /> <br /> <b>Awakening</b><br /> There\u2019s this thing often termed The Trials. Roughly every 27 years in their life, sorcerers experience a time where their magic and senses heighten significantly. The first time this happens is generally the all-or-nothing point of a sorcerer\u2019s life where they either accept their magic or lose it.<br /> <br /> For the weakly-gifted (just like any other talent, there\u2019s variance among sorcerers), this time doesn\u2019t make as much fuss. For the more strongly-gifted though, it\u2019s a lot more stressful. Combine a strong sorcerer and a society that says they shouldn\u2019t believe in their magic, the results can be devastating.<br /> <br /> Sounds quite a bit like Awakening, doesn\u2019t it?<br /> <br /> <b>Mage Sight</b><br /> This is actually a real talent. Granted, it\u2019s nothing like what\u2019s described in the game. It\u2019s simply a general sense of magic. It\u2019s also not something every sorcerer has, in fact, it\u2019s pretty rare. Still, it\u2019s very much a thing in real magic.<br /> <br /> <b>High Speech</b><br /> Like Mage Sight, this is also very much a thing in real magic, although it\u2019s entirely different from what\u2019s described in the game. In real magic, High Speech are particular words sorcerers say when casting spells. What the words are varies from individual to individual, as it\u2019s purely instinctual. My High Speech is going to be very different from another sorcerer\u2019s High Speech (I don\u2019t know mine yet, and I don\u2019t know when I\u2019ll learn them; like most things with magic, it comes when it comes).<br /> <br /> <b>Yantras</b><br /> Remember when I said Spirited Away is essentially an instruction manual for magic? Well, what instruction manual would be complete without teaching a common spell? In the film\u2019s case, it teaches engacho, a spell used to dispel negative influences.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://pa1.narvii.com/5590/387cd8c29237258877266ede035a1b6cf704b7d9_hq.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> When Chihiro puts her fingers together, she\u2019s performing a real-life equivalent of a Yantra. She\u2019s channelling the idea of containing the negative influence into the space of her fingers, and when Kamaji chops her gesture apart, he\u2019s channelling the idea of destroying the influence, which is why he says \u201cEvil begone.\u201d as he does it.<br /> <br /> One well-known example, and one that relates more directly to the game itself, is the Tarot deck. Each card represents certain concepts and you put them into a certain context in spreads, which allows a sorcerer to read a specific message from the cards they drew, their talent guiding them to draw the right cards.<br /> <br /> <b>Wisdom &amp; Paradox</b><br /> The way of magic is often termed as the Way of the Wise, and for very good reason. Magic isn\u2019t a plaything; it\u2019s a powerful force, like fire or electricity. Misused, it can harm you, maybe even kill you. It\u2019s something you need to control, otherwise you\u2019re gonna make a huge mess; and not just for you, but for a lot of others.<br /> <br /> Being a horror game, Mage: the Awakening focuses on this particular aspect of magic and makes it a lot more horrible. After all, that\u2019s what horror is supposed to do, it shows us the darker aspects, often by exaggerating them or at the very least fully exposing them. Real magic doesn\u2019t tear away at people\u2019s sanity in the manner that Awakening magic does, but it can still do some serious damage nonetheless.<br /> <br /> <b>Conclusion</b><br /> Mage: the Awakening, at least for me, but probably for a lot of other sorcerers out there, says that magic is real, that our senses aren\u2019t lying to us. It tends to focus on where magic can go wrong, but that\u2019s simply part and parcel with a horror game, and it\u2019s a valuable lesson besides.<br /> <br /> What\u2019s even better is that it doesn\u2019t just relate to sorcerers, it can relate to just about anyone. Magic can simply be an analogy for potential and the consequences our actions can have in a generic sense, not just in the specific context of real magic. To think before you act is a valuable lesson for anyone to heed. It just so happens to resonate more strongly for sorcerers in particular, in a similar vein to The Matrix, a film that audiences worldwide can relate to on some level, but hits home a lot more for trans people, because it was made by trans people.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t doubt for a second that at least one developer of the game has the gift; there\u2019s just so much that aligns with my experiences in real magic. Just as there\u2019s so much in The Matrix that aligns with trans people. So, if any of you guys are reading this: thank you, and excellent work. If I\u2019m wrong about that, though, still kudos to you for your outstanding research.<br /> <br /> And for those who find this entire OP to be ridiculous: well, at least we can all agree that Mage: the Awakening is an awesome game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-22T08:47:51-07:00","id":1095499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>crapcarp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1095458-why-m-taw-resonates-with-me-and-probably-several-others#post1095458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, I am not someone who dabbles in New Age mumbo-jumbo mistaken as occult practices, I use real magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're not really selling that seeing as your references are Star Wars and Spirited Away.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don\u2019t doubt for a second that at least one developer of the game has the gift; there\u2019s just so much that aligns with my experiences in real magic. </div> </div> </div>More seriously, they probably just read a lot. Like, the 1e core has recommendations for non-fiction books on magic, and those things you describe are all aspects of historical occult and religious practices. Awakening is basically lots of real life occultism stitched together into a game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There\u2019s this thing often termed The Trials. </div> </div> </div>Okay, but there are major religions that use the metaphor of awakening when referring to seeing through the illusion on the world.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-22T10:53:17-07:00","id":1095557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1095458-why-m-taw-resonates-with-me-and-probably-several-others?p=1095499#post1095499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're not really selling that seeing as your references are Star Wars and Spirited Away.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> More seriously, they probably just read a lot. Like, the 1e core has recommendations for non-fiction books on magic, and those things you describe are all aspects of historical occult and religious practices. Awakening is basically lots of real life occultism stitched together into a game.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Okay, but there are major religions that use the metaphor of awakening when referring to seeing through the illusion on the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Crapcarp's point is less to convince you and more to simply tell you why he likes the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-22T19:41:30-07:00","id":1095723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Falcon777</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1095458-why-m-taw-resonates-with-me-and-probably-several-others?p=1095557#post1095557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think Crapcarp's point is less to convince you and more to simply tell you why he likes the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is plenty interesting and worthwhile in its own right. Thanks for sharing, OP.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/747-knowbody","name":"Knowbody","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-22T20:26:42-07:00","id":1095735,"title":"","content":"Look, I'm not opposed to belief systems that allow for the possibility of magic. My partner is pagan. But, I have two gripes here: one is that the comparison to moles is really condescending. The comparison to Awakening's sleepers is moreso. Just because the experiences you describe are not what I would call &quot;magic&quot; doesn't make me incapable of perceiving the same things that you are. Second, Chronicles (and to a greater extent, World) of Darkness has some really unfortunate history with fans taking the &quot;this is real&quot; thing too far, and given that context, I don't think these forums are an appropriate place to discuss the resemblance between the magic you believe to be real and the games Onyx Path develops. Though note that I am saying that in black, non-mod text.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-22T20:32:04-07:00","id":1095738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1095458-why-m-taw-resonates-with-me-and-probably-several-others?p=1095499#post1095499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're not really selling that seeing as your references are Star Wars and Spirited Away.</div> </div> </div> </div>For starters, neither Star Wars or Spirited Away derive from New Age concepts, and even if they did, that's besides the point. It's a case of art imitating life and also giving people an idea of what I'm talking about (y'know the Force from Star Wars, it's kinda like that, just without the purely fantastical elements like force gripping or lightning from fingers).<br /> <br /> \u200bI suggest reading up on New Age material, you'll find that what I'm describing doesn't correlate with it at all, or if it does, it's rare and very minor (a stopped clock is right twice a day, after all).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1095458-why-m-taw-resonates-with-me-and-probably-several-others?p=1095499#post1095499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">More seriously, they probably just read a lot. Like, the 1e core has recommendations for non-fiction books on magic, and those things you describe are all aspects of historical occult and religious practices. Awakening is basically lots of real life occultism stitched together into a game.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's entirely possible. Like I said before, if that is indeed the case, it's clear that they did some seriously good and deep research on it, and they deserve praise for that. The thing is, it aligns so completely and so well to my experiences that I wouldn't be surprised if at least one of the developers also happens to be a sorcerer. Life experience counts for a lot, after all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1095458-why-m-taw-resonates-with-me-and-probably-several-others?p=1095499#post1095499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, but there are major religions that use the metaphor of awakening when referring to seeing through the illusion on the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, and that's no coincidence. Most religions have certain magical practices as a component, Christianity in particular.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-22T21:18:59-07:00","id":1095748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1095458-why-m-taw-resonates-with-me-and-probably-several-others?p=1095735#post1095735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Look, I'm not opposed to belief systems that allow for the possibility of magic. My partner is pagan. But, I have two gripes here: one is that the comparison to moles is really condescending. The comparison to Awakening's sleepers is moreso.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI apologise, that was not my intent.<br /> <br /> The mole analogy wasn't meant to be diminutive, just noting a particular perspective is all. Not &quot;you're just a lowly mole&quot; but rather &quot;moles can't see stars, that's why it's rational for them to disbelieve that they exist&quot;. That's why I included the whole &quot;sorcerers just have different talents, like everyone else&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1095458-why-m-taw-resonates-with-me-and-probably-several-others?p=1095735#post1095735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just because the experiences you describe are not what I would call &quot;magic&quot; doesn't make me incapable of perceiving the same things that you are.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bOkay, now I see why you got offended: I wasn't entirely clear. When I talk about disbelief, I'm not talking about those, like you, who simply don't call what I describe as magic. There are several names for it. Native Americans often referred to it as medicine, some people call it psychic powers, I and my mentor call it magic. Different names for the same thing.<br /> <br /> \u200bWhat I was referring to with disbelief are those who outright say things like &quot;Magic/psychic powers/etc. isn't real&quot; or &quot;it's all just a bunch of New Age bullshit&quot;. Sorry I wasn't clear in my OP.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1095458-why-m-taw-resonates-with-me-and-probably-several-others?p=1095735#post1095735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Second, Chronicles (and to a greater extent, World) of Darkness has some really unfortunate history with fans taking the &quot;this is real&quot; thing too far, and given that context, I don't think these forums are an appropriate place to discuss the resemblance between the magic you believe to be real and the games Onyx Path develops. Though note that I am saying that in black, non-mod text.</div> </div> </div> </div>I personally disagree with that. I do note your concern, though, and I will agree that it needs to be taken into account with these discussions. Mage: the Awakening, like Star Wars and Spirited Away, is a case of art imitating life. But, as with all art imitating life, it isn't a perfect mirror. All three have some fantastical elements to them, and they need to be accounted for. The Force, conceptually speaking, is a great metaphor for the nature of magic, but magic is never going to allow you to choke someone with you mind or allow you to sprout lightning from your fingers, those are just the fantastical elements.<br /> <br /> \u200bMage: the Awakening is much the same, and I have noted some dissimilarities, such as the physical world not being an illusion or a non-sorcerer not going insane by seeing someone work magic. Like I said in the OP, much of the game's fantastical elements are outright horrible, and purposely so because that's the whole point of horror. So don't worry, I've taken your concern into account when I started this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-23T00:14:13-07:00","id":1095782,"title":"","content":"If MtAw teaches anything about or is derived from magic/faith/ideology in real life (I consider them nigh same), it's probably Gnosticism.<br /> <br /> EDIT: With a healthy dose of humanism, making the Fallen and imperfect world and its Sleeping residents worth on their own. To deny it is the first step to Hubris, at least in Mage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":12619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","user":"21C Hermit","date":". 05-23-2017, 03:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-23T01:39:18-07:00","id":1095798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>crapcarp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1095458-why-m-taw-resonates-with-me-and-probably-several-others?p=1095738#post1095738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For starters, neither Star Wars or Spirited Away derive from New Age concepts, and even if they did, that's besides the point. It's a case of art imitating life and also giving people an idea of what I'm talking about (y'know the Force from Star Wars, it's kinda like that, just without the purely fantastical elements like force gripping or lightning from fingers).<br /> <br /> \u200bI suggest reading up on New Age material, you'll find that what I'm describing doesn't correlate with it at all, or if it does, it's rare and very minor (a stopped clock is right twice a day, after all).</div> </div> </div> </div>My point is that you're asking to be taken seriously, whilst showing fairly massive disrespect for other people's beliefs.<br /> <br /> Also, I'm not a believer in magic, but I have a passing familiarity with real life occultism and the terms you've used sound like nothing I've ever heard of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-23T03:20:06-07:00","id":1095817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1095458-why-m-taw-resonates-with-me-and-probably-several-others?p=1095798#post1095798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I'm not a believer in magic, but I have a passing familiarity with real life occultism and the terms you've used sound like nothing I've ever heard of.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bBack when I was untrained, I too had a passing familiarity with real life occultism. Much of the stuff I've described was completely new to me once I started training, so you not hearing about it doesn't surprise me, I was in the same boat.<br /> <br /> \u200bThing is, the truth of the occult has been buried under tons of smearing propaganda, snake oil, wishful thinking, and sometimes even straight up wild guessing. When you have to contend with all that, how can anyone blame you for not knowing? I certainly can't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-23T03:35:59-07:00","id":1095820,"title":"","content":"I really don't think that OPP forum is a place to talk about occult from a perspective of a believer. Role playing games have a history of being associated with 'satanic' practices and thread like this don't help that cause. You can believe in anything you want but using phrases like 'I'm more aware then you', 'I too have been where you are' is too close to indoctrinating cult practices.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":1747,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","user":"Moinen","date":". 05-23-2017, 06:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-23T03:42:47-07:00","id":1095821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>crapcarp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1095458-why-m-taw-resonates-with-me-and-probably-several-others?p=1095817#post1095817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bBack when I was untrained, I too had a passing familiarity with real life occultism. Much of the stuff I've described was completely new to me once I started training, so you not hearing about it doesn't surprise me, I was in the same boat.<br /> <br /> \u200bThing is, the truth of the occult has been buried under tons of smearing propaganda, snake oil, wishful thinking, and sometimes even straight up wild guessing. When you have to contend with all that, how can anyone blame you for not knowing? I certainly can't.</div> </div> </div> </div>Be careful where you tread, good sir or madam. Without something like the Sleeping Curse or the Technocracy, the only reason occultism, mysticism, and esoterica are being shunned in real life is because of their insularity and elitism.<br /> <br /> In fact, I'm sure many of us here would appreciate you sharing what you've gleaned and compare it with how MtAw describes magic. Because this is, after all, a Mage forum.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-23T03:57:26-07:00","id":1095823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1095458-why-m-taw-resonates-with-me-and-probably-several-others?p=1095821#post1095821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In fact, I'm sure many of us here would appreciate you sharing what you've gleaned and compare it with how MtAw describes magic. Because this is, after all, a Mage forum.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't, any more than I'd appreciate a devout Christian telling me all about the similarities between their beliefs and the God-Machine, and comparing people like me to subterranean rodents in the process.<br /> <br /> Moinen hit the nail on the head.<br /> <br /> This isn't the place for an AMA from someone who believes they're a real-life Mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-23T04:16:49-07:00","id":1095828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1095458-why-m-taw-resonates-with-me-and-probably-several-others?p=1095823#post1095823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't, any more than I'd appreciate a devout Christian telling me all about the similarities between their beliefs and the God-Machine, and comparing people like me to subterranean rodents in the process.<br /> <br /> Moinen hit the nail on the head.<br /> <br /> This isn't the place for an AMA from someone who believes they're a real-life Mage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Looks like my nuance from my tongue got lost in the keyboard. I meant that any talks of real-life mysticism should be related to Mage, because this is a Mage forum.<br /> <br /> Comparing other people to moles is something I also do not appreciate. Like I said (or at least, meant to say) in the part of my post that you didn't quote, mystics in reality get a bad rep whenever some other guy claims he is better than all the clueless masses out there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-23T04:19:53-07:00","id":1095829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1095458-why-m-taw-resonates-with-me-and-probably-several-others?p=1095828#post1095828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">any talks of real-life mysticism should be related to Mage, because this is a Mage forum.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see your meaning, now - but I don't think talks of real-life mysticism belong here at all. We have an off-topic forum.<br /> <br /> OPP has done a really good job of distancing the practices and beliefs of things in their fictional settings from real world counterparts, especially compared to OWOD. I think that separation is a good thing, and should carry over to their discussion forums, personally.<br /> <br /> As for the quote - sorry, I try to just quote the parts I'm responding too - consider the rest of your message received.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}